From 228e85fc276772c548ff55c1595132bbc054d64d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:26:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] test(sdk/contracts): re-point the v0.13.0 cleartext mock at
 the ACL v0.4.1 backport

CleartextACL (src/v0.13.0/cleartext/CleartextACL.sol) inherits the vendored
host-contracts ACL by relative path (CleartextACL.sol:4), so a remapping
cannot redirect it. This commit replaces the two vendored files with
byte-identical copies of the v0.13 line's Level 0 backport (61be560):

- src/v0.13.0/host-contracts/contracts/ACL.sol       <- host-contracts/contracts/ACL.sol (ACL v0.4.1)
- src/v0.13.0/host-contracts/contracts/ACLEvents.sol <- host-contracts/contracts/ACLEvents.sol

Every other file the backport imports (shared/UUPSUpgradeableEmptyProxy.sol,
interfaces/IPauserSet.sol, OpenZeppelin 5.1.0) is already identical in the
vendored tree; ../addresses/FHEVMHostAddresses.sol stays the mock's own
address file, so FHEVM_EXECUTOR_ADDRESS keeps pointing at the mock executor.
Changing CleartextACL's import to ../../../../../../host-contracts/... was not
used: it would pull host-contracts/addresses/ (generated, git-ignored, other
addresses) into the mock.

CleartextACL.sol itself is unchanged and overrides neither persistAllowed,
isAllowed nor isHandleDelegatedForUserDecryption, so its user and delegated
decryption views (CleartextACL.sol:236, :239, :257) now run the backport's
retirement gates. The vendored copy was the v0.13.0-x pre-release ACL v0.4.0
(delegation expiry `>=`); the backport is built from the v0.13.8 tag (`>`).

Test-only mock code (never deployed to production networks).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
